# The host's reset dance, after the application has booted.
#
# `download-mode` is M6's decoding of an esptool "reset into the download
# console" sequence, applied at a slice boundary and stamped with the guest
# cycle. Until M7 the machine could only report it: there was no boot chain
# to reboot into. With `--merged --reboot-on-reset` the request is performed,
# and the log has two boots in it — the second one the ROM's own console.
# Well past `[INIT] fw-esp32 initialized`, so the reset lands on a running
# application rather than on the bootloader.
# Times are EMULATED MILLISECONDS.
1200 download-mode
